- data = language_data
%main.language-map-page
  %h2.mb-2 Los Angeles Area Languages
  %p.language-map-intro
    Where English learners who speak each language go to school.
    Pick a language to see it on the big map, then use the slider to see how it has changed since 2011.
  .language-map-layout
    %section.language-panel#language-panel{ aria: { label: 'Selected language' }, data: { language: data.to_json, year: @year } }
      %h3.language-title
        %span.language-title-endonym#language-title-endonym{ lang: data[:lang], dir: 'auto', hidden: data[:endonym].nil? }= data[:endonym]
        %span#language-title-name= @language.name
      %p.school-language-total
        %strong#school-language-total-count= number_with_delimiter(data[:totals][@years.index(@year)])
        English learners spoke
        %span#school-language-total-name= @language.name
        at home in
        %span#school-language-total-year= SchoolLanguage.school_year(@year)
      .school-language-year
        %label.form-label.visually-hidden{ for: 'school-language-year' } School year
        %button.btn.btn-sm.btn-outline-secondary#school-language-play{ type: 'button' } Play
        %input.form-range#school-language-year{ type: 'range', min: 0, max: @years.size - 1, step: 1, value: @years.index(@year), aria: { valuetext: SchoolLanguage.school_year(@year) } }
        %strong#school-language-year-label= SchoolLanguage.school_year(@year)
      .school-language-map
      .school-language-trend#school-language-trend{ role: 'list', aria: { label: 'English learners by school year' } }
        - max = [data[:totals].max.to_i, 1].max
        - @years.each_with_index do |year, index|
          - total = data[:totals][index]
          %button.trend-bar{ type: 'button', role: 'listitem', class: ('selected' if year == @year), data: { index: index },
                             title: "#{SchoolLanguage.school_year(year)}: #{number_with_delimiter(total)}",
                             aria: { label: "#{SchoolLanguage.school_year(year)}: #{number_with_delimiter(total)} English learners" } }
            %span.trend-fill{ style: "height: #{(100.0 * total / max).round(1)}%" }
            %span.trend-year= "'#{format('%02d', year % 100)}"
      %details.top-schools
        %summary
          Schools with the most English learners who speak
          %span#school-language-table-name= @language.name
        %table.table.table-sm.school-language-schools
          %thead
            %tr
              %th School
              %th District
              %th.text-end Students
          %tbody#school-language-schools
    %section.language-wall{ aria: { label: 'Languages' } }
      .browse-controls
        %input.form-control#language-search{ type: 'search', placeholder: 'Find a language', aria: { label: 'Find a language' } }
        .btn-group{ role: 'group', aria: { label: 'Sort languages' } }
          %button.btn.btn-sm.btn-outline-secondary.active{ type: 'button', data: { sort: 'size' }, aria: { pressed: 'true' } } Largest
          %button.btn.btn-sm.btn-outline-secondary{ type: 'button', data: { sort: 'name' }, aria: { pressed: 'false' } } A–Z
      %p.browse-empty#language-search-empty{ hidden: true } No language matches.
      = render 'footprints'
  .school-language-notes
    %p
      These are
      %strong English learners,
      students still learning English, so they aren't everyone who speaks a language.
      Students who are fluent in English aren't counted, so languages spoken mostly by recent immigrants show up more than long-established ones.
    %p
      Source:
      = link_to('California Department of Education, English Learners by Grade & Language', 'https://www.cde.ca.gov/ds/ad/fileselsch.asp', target: '_blank', rel: 'noopener')
      for public schools in Los Angeles, Orange, Ventura, Riverside, and San Bernardino counties.
      CDE changed its language codes in 2023-24, so a few related languages are grouped together to keep years comparable.
      County outlines from the
      = succeed('.') do
        = link_to('California Department of Technology', 'https://gis.data.ca.gov/datasets/CDT::california-county-boundaries-and-identifiers', target: '_blank', rel: 'noopener')
